    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just a \"setback\" though. everything i've built, my whole identity... it was all based on being the one who succeeds. now i'm just the person who failed. my parents didn't just invest in me, they relied on me to be this perfect version of myself. i feel like i've let them down so deeply that there's no way to come back from it. it feels like the person they loved doesn't even exist anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable that you feel like your entire identity is crumbling when the foundation you built it on has cracked. The pressure you felt to be perfect was immense, and it's okay to feel the weight of that expectation now. Remember that your worth is inherent, separate from any achievement or external validation. Perhaps talking to a counselor could help you begin to separate who you are from what you accomplished.",
      "source": "target",
